-- title:
--   Rank of a non-Eisenstein corner of H¹(Γ_H(M),𝒪)
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation ring (a domain), let $k$ be a field which is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra such that the structure map $\mathcal{O}\to k$ is surjective, let $M'\ge 1$, let $H'\le(\mathbb{Z}/M')^\times$ be a subgroup and let $S$ be a finite set of natural numbers. On $H^1 = \operatorname{Hom}(\Gamma_{H'}(M'),\mathcal{O})$, the additive homomorphisms from the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_{H'}(M')\le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ to $\mathcal{O}$, the family [`CohCarrier.opFamily`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L91) attaches to each generator symbol in [`CohCarrier.Gen`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13) an $\mathcal{O}$-endomorphism: to $T_\ell$ for a prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid M'$ and to $U_q$ for a prime $q\mid M'$ the transfer operator [`CohCarrier.heckeTL`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L23), and to $d\in(\mathbb{Z}/M')^\times$ the diamond operator. Assume these endomorphisms commute pairwise, and let $\bar\theta$ be an arbitrary $k$-valued function on the generator symbols. Let $\mathbb{T}$ be the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathcal{O}}(H^1)$ generated by this family, and let $S'$ be an idempotent splitting of $\mathbb{T}$: complete orthogonal idempotents $e_0,\dots,e_{n-1}$ together with maximal ideals $\mathfrak{m}_i$ exhausting the maximal ideals of $\mathbb{T}$ and satisfying $e_i\in\mathfrak{m}_j \iff i\ne j$. Fix an index $i_0$ and an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra homomorphism $\pi\colon e_{i_0}\mathbb{T}e_{i_0}\to k$ with $\pi(e_{i_0}\,T\,e_{i_0}) = \bar\theta(g)$ for every generator symbol $g$ with operator $T$. Assume the non-Eisenstein condition: there is a prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid M'$ and $\ell\equiv 1 \pmod{M'}$ such that $\bar\theta(T_\ell)\ne \ell+1$ in $k$. Then the $\mathcal{O}$-rank of the corner submodule $e_{i_0}\cdot H^1$, the range of multiplication by $e_{i_0}$ on $H^1$, equals $2\cdot\operatorname{rank}_{\mathcal{O}}\bigl(e_{i_0}\mathbb{T}e_{i_0}\bigr)$.
--
--   This is the "rank two" statement for group cohomology of $\Gamma_H(M)$ with coefficients in a discrete valuation ring: after localising at a maximal ideal of the Hecke algebra whose associated system of eigenvalues is not Eisenstein, $H^1$ becomes of rank exactly $2$ over the local Hecke algebra. It is used in the project to produce the Galois action on the ordinary line modulo the corner submodule and to deduce freeness of that corner submodule under absolute irreducibility and ordinarity hypotheses.
